| `tests/integration/test_realness_gate.py` | Fails, at its file, line and function, a test function under the realness roots whose tier is `mock`, naming the signal that put it there, so an e2e test never passes against a programmed double of the dependency it claims to drive. `tests/realness.py` puts a test in the lowest tier among its signals (`mock` < `fake` < `in_process` < `real`, or `unknown` with none): a use of a name an import binds to a library `tests/realness_data.py` tiers, each fixture it requests by parameter or `@pytest.mark.usefixtures`, resolved module first and then each `conftest.py` up to the root, through the fixtures those request, and each autouse fixture of that chain. A run over zero test functions and a stale excuse fail too. | `make test` | [`test_quality.realness.roots`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`test_quality.realness.exempt.<test>`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | It reads the syntax tree and never runs a test. A class-level `usefixtures`, a `pytest_plugins` module and a fixture defined in a class are not read, and a library or fixture absent from `tests/realness_data.py` contributes nothing. Not proof that a test reaches real infrastructure: `unknown` and `in_process` pass. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
